e","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It mostly just seemed proper, since we wouldn't in fact have run any constructor for them at all otherwise, which (as I [recently](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107832#discussion_r2172983542) learned myself) is considered undefined behavior according to the C++ standard:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"815\" height=\"117\" alt=\"C++ standard quote\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a96d905d-67e8-4b54-bb16-ee078dc8ec51\" />\r\n\r\nFor what it's worth, Clang (with `lto=thin`) seems to inline the three of these just fine, into these instructions:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"312\" height=\"92\" alt=\"Assembly code\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e75930c7-f970-4345-9a78-ab0663dc461a\" />\r\n\r\nI can move the `ADDR_STACK_SELF` constructor call into the `p_instance` case if you want, but it has no effect at all in our real-world benchmark.","created_at":"2026-03-26T14:53:57Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T14:53:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#discussion_r2995575279","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117850","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2995575279"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117850#discussion_r2995575279"},"pull_request":{"href":"htt